{"ok":true,"result":{"id":"request-6","jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"content":[{"text":"<instruction>\n# Capability and owner\n\nSelect from the actual requested outcome, preserving valid explicit ownership. Do not reconstruct the full expert catalog after a route is resolved.\n\nIF ShipGlows-owned skill/doctrine audit? SELECT shipglows/core_audit and LOAD the original Core owner, selected audit pack and fidelity contract. Audit findings do not authorize repair. An explicit Core invocation binds its remaining scope to ShipGlows, including quoted application evidence.\nIF internal architecture/governance/context/metadata/agent documentation? SELECT sg-docs and LOAD original docs owner/selected governance workflow after canonical and invocation checks. Internal documentation and public audience content have different owners.\nIF public documentation/editorial/audience output? SELECT sg-content and LOAD original content owner/selected source, quality and delivery contracts. Resolve product, audience and public surface. A short conversational summary retains the content owner; use a drafting helper only when substantive drafting actually triggers it.\nIF private pointer/bookmark/persistence or declared private namespace access? SELECT sg-private for that bounded private capability and LOAD original private owner/root/data contracts. For private-to-public work, content retains the public outcome while the private capability controls access; neither replaces the other's protections.\nIF requested explanation of skills/modes/workflows/prompts? Explain directly while action remains excluded. Use original help references only for the requested fact. Actionable work transitions to its outcome owner in this conversation, preserving authority; a help answer does not own mutations or trackers.\n\nFor each selected owner verify its original canonical engine identity; missing identity or required validation STOP. Public names remain public; internal engines stay out of ordinary user reports. Original domain leaves, source/rubric proof, reporting and governance remain authoritative. Requests outside these bounded experimental capabilities exit visibly or use an available canonical route; never guess permission or a missing resource.\n\n</instruction>","type":"text"}],"isError":false}}}
